// A closure-valued parameter spelled `__store_string__`, called in the body. The name is bound
// by the program, so the call denotes the parameter and nothing about the memory intrinsic is
// reachable from it — a legal program. The checker refused it with `'__store_string__' is
// declared but has no implementation yet`, because the gate asked the flat top-level function
// table whether the program declared that name and a PARAMETER is not in that table.
//
// Two ingredients, each necessary: the name being one `nameIsUnimplementedIntrinsic` answers for
// (any other spelling always ran), and the shadowing binding being something other than a
// top-level `function` of that name, which the gate did see. See D1604.
// Should print 3.
function tak(__store_string__: (i32, i32) => void) { __store_string__(1, 2) }
tak((a, b) => {
  print(a + b)
})
